# Block Conventions

This rule covers **editing** an existing block. For scaffolding a new one, use
`.cursor/skills/sf-blocks/`.

## Static or dynamic

| `save.js` returns markup | `save.js` returns `null` |
|---|---|
| Content known at edit time | Content depends on database, user, or request |
| No `render` key in `block.json` | `"render": "file:./render.php"` |

Returning `null` without a `render` key produces a block that renders nothing on
the frontend and gives no error. Changing a static block's markup invalidates
existing content — expect block validation warnings and plan a deprecation.

## Where block PHP may live

`build:blocks` passes `--webpack-copy-php`, so every `.php` file beside
`block.json` is copied into `build-jsx-blocks/`. Default `wp-scripts`
copies only the `render` file; the flag lifts that.

- Block-local PHP may live next to `block.json`.
- Anything shared with a hook, REST route, `lib/` class, or another block
  goes in `includes/{capability}/`, and `render.php` calls it as a thin
  shim.

Most commerce blocks here are still shims of that second kind. Do not
relocate existing `includes/` helpers into a block folder just because
the copy flag exists.

## In `render.php`

```php
$wrapper = get_block_wrapper_attributes();                  // never hand-build the class string
$mine    = get_field( 'block_setting' );                    // the block's own field group
$post    = get_field( 'post_setting', get_the_ID() );        // the post — ID is required
```

Escape all output. Guard plugin-dependent code: block registration is
directory-driven and does **not** check whether the plugin exists.

## Attributes

Declare every attribute in `block.json` with an explicit `type`. When an attribute
has a non-empty `default`, an "empty" value must be set explicitly in content or
the default leaks through — this bites when authoring patterns. Check `block.json`
before assuming an omitted attribute renders blank.

## Editor code

Functional components with hooks. Prefer `@wordpress/components` and
`@wordpress/block-editor` over hand-rolled UI. Wrap user-facing strings in
`@wordpress/i18n` with the `skaflow` text domain.

## Frontend behaviour

Add `view.js` and declare `viewScript` in `block.json`. **Anything touching a card,
swatch, or grid item must be delegated** — direct `addEventListener` works on page
one and breaks silently after Load More or a filter refresh. See
`.cursor/rules/sf-event-delegation.mdc`.

## Styles

Per-block `style.scss` / `editor.scss` are for JSX blocks only; ACF blocks style
from `src/sass/`. Content styles must enqueue on `enqueue_block_assets`, not
`enqueue_block_editor_assets`, or they won't reach the editor iframe.

## After changing a block

```bash
cd wp-content/themes/skaflow && npm run build:blocks
```

Source-only changes never register — the registry reads `build-jsx-blocks/`.

